implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST (red). Load test-driven-development. NEVER run npm test, npm run build/clean or tsc in the shared checkout's packages/moe-proxy. The global moe-proxy command is an npm link to it, so every live WSL seat runs its gitignored dist, and pretest's clean deletes dist first (mem:gotcha-proxy-npm-test-shared-checkout-deletes-dist). Every test run happens in a git-archive snapshot.

Before editing:
- Run `git diff --quiet HEAD -- packages/moe-proxy/src/utils.ts packages/moe-proxy/src/utils.test.ts`. Both files were clean at plan time; if either is dirty, read planningNotes.risks before touching it.
- Record `stat -c '%Y %s' packages/moe-proxy/dist/index.js` for step 3.

In packages/moe-proxy/src/utils.test.ts, describe('comparableProjectPath') (~line 210):
- Add `afterEach(() => { vi.restoreAllMocks(); });` at the top of the block (vi and afterEach are already imported).
- Append two tests after 'does not equate different projects'. Copy the shape of the daemon's X9/X10 (packages/moe-daemon/src/index.test.ts ~lines 374-407), which pin the same rule there.

(T1) POSIX only, `it.skipIf(process.platform === 'win32')`, named 'maps /mnt/<d> after resolving relative and non-normalized paths'.
- `vi.spyOn(process, 'cwd').mockReturnValue('/mnt/d/x')` stands in for a WSL cwd: posix path.resolve reads process.cwd() on every call, and chdir is unavailable in vitest workers.
- Assert through one table, so a failure names its input:
  const same = ['.', '/mnt/d/x/.', '/mnt/d/x/sub/..', '/mnt/d//x', 'sub/..', '/mnt/d/x/./', '/mnt/d/x', 'D:\\x'];
  expect(same.map((p) => [p, comparableProjectPath(p)])).toEqual(same.map((p) => [p, 'd:/x']));
  expect(['sub', '..'].map((p) => [p, comparableProjectPath(p)])).toEqual([['sub', 'd:/x/sub'], ['..', 'd:']]);

(T2) Every platform, named 'on win32 posix-normalizes a raw /mnt/<d> path before mapping it'. Add a local synchronous helper onWin32<T>(fn: () => T): T. On real win32 it just returns fn(). Otherwise it:
- saves Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(process, 'platform') and redefines it with value 'win32';
- spies path.resolve with mockImplementation((...parts: string[]) => path.win32.resolve('C:\\work', ...parts));
- restores both in a finally (mockRestore, then the saved descriptor).
Flipping the platform alone is not enough. Posix path.resolve of an absolute /mnt path is already normalized, so a mutant that resolves instead of posix-normalizing would pass (mem:gotcha-comparable-project-path-relative). Assert:
  const rows = ['/mnt/d/x/sub/..', '/mnt/d/x/./', '/mnt/d//x', 'D:\\x'];
  expect(onWin32(() => rows.map((p) => [p, comparableProjectPath(p)]))).toEqual(rows.map((p) => [p, 'd:/x']));
  expect(onWin32(() => comparableProjectPath('/mnt/d/x/sub/../..'))).toBe('d:');

RED proof, in a snapshot:
- ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel); SNAP=$(mktemp -d /tmp/moe-ea57-red.XXXXXX)
- git -C "$ROOT" archive HEAD packages/moe-proxy | tar -x -C "$SNAP"
- Copy the edited utils.test.ts over the snapshot's copy and cmp the two.
- (cd "$SNAP/packages/moe-proxy" && npm ci --no-audit --no-fund && npx vitest run src/utils.test.ts)
On HEAD's utils.ts, T1 and T2 must fail and every other test in the file must pass. HEAD gives:
- '/mnt/d/x' for '.';
- 'd:/x/.' for '/mnt/d/x/.';
- 'd:/x/sub/..' for '/mnt/d/x/sub/..';
- 'd://x' for '/mnt/d//x'.
Record the failing test names and the observed values in the step note.

If vitest dies with 'Cannot find native binding', apply the rolldown fallback in mem:gotcha-gate-snapshot-psparse-and-proxy-rolldown: npm pack the lock's @rolldown/binding-linux-x64-gnu, check its integrity, and extract it into node_modules. Never edit package-lock.json. Keep $SNAP for step 2.
